    "title": "Top View of a Binary Tree",
    "category": "Trees",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "problemStatement": "Given the root of a binary tree, determine the set of nodes visible when the tree is viewed from the top. For every vertical column, only the first visible node should be included.",
